WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.202
Validation should normally happen before correction.

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:07.167
This query checks product prices and assigns a status.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.782
A missing price is labeled missing.

00:00:09.782 --> 00:00:15.622
A price less than or equal to zero is labeled invalid and marked for review.

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:18.106
Anything else becomes a valid candidate.

00:00:18.756 --> 00:00:21.343
The important word again is candidate.

00:00:21.343 --> 00:00:27.203
A positive number satisfies our selected rule, but it may still be wrong.

00:00:27.203 --> 00:00:36.278
A product that normally costs twenty dollars could accidentally be entered as two thousand dollars and still pass this

00:00:36.278 --> 00:00:40.098
simple check. Validation only tests the rules we define.

00:00:40.098 --> 00:00:43.278
So begin with clear, transparent checks.

00:00:43.278 --> 00:00:45.838
Identify the records that fail.

00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:49.338
Then decide what to do with them based on evidence.

00:00:49.338 --> 00:00:54.380
This is much safer than immediately changing every value that looks unusual.
